  "question": "What does the Jabal Dabub inscription say?",
  "answer": "The Jabal Ḏabūb inscription is a South Arabian graffito in Late Sabaic [S3]. Its text reads, in transliteration, \"bs¹mlh | rḥmn | rḥmn | rb | s¹mwt / r{z}{q}n | mfḍlk | wʾṯrn | mḫh | s²kmt ʾymn\" [S3]. According to the published translation supplied with this source, it says: \"In the name of Allah, the Rahman — have mercy upon us, O lord of the heavens; satisfy us by means of your favor; and grant us the essence of it at the end/gift of our days\" [S3].",
